From: plutoplus_dvb
Subject: [PATCH] tsinput: do not bind the same UDP address twice

pluto_dvb sends tx/dvbs2/tssourceaddress every time it starts, so each
start added another SO_REUSEADDR socket on 127.0.0.1:1314. The datagrams
then went to an old socket that nothing reads, and the encoder sent only
padding packets (PID 0x1FFE).

---
--- a/tsinputmux.cpp	2026-11-09 18:32:08
+++ b/tsinputmux.cpp	2026-11-09 18:32:08
@@ -1484,6 +1484,10 @@
     case tssource_udp:
     {
         if (arg == NULL)
+            break;
+        // Binding the same address again leaves several SO_REUSEADDR sockets
+        // on the port, and the datagrams may go to one nothing reads.
+        if (recv_ts_sock > 0 && strcmp(m_mcast_ts, arg) == 0)
             break;
         strcpy(m_mcast_ts, arg);
         fprintf(stderr, "Try udp %s\n", m_mcast_ts);
